          "text": "Not a UFO but, how damn cool is this?! A blue banded blood moon from Sep. 7, 2025. \n\nWhat exactly are we looking at though? The “blue band” on a blood moon is a brief effect that can appear during a total lunar eclipse. Sunlight grazing Earth’s atmosphere is filtered by stratospheric ozone, which absorbs red wavelengths and lets more blue through. \n\nThat bluish light can tint a narrow, turquoise-like arc on the Moon. It is real but typically faint and is easiest to see in contrast-enhanced images.\n#ufotwitter #ufox"
